  "worked_solution": "First, recall that:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{s\\to 0}f(s)=\u27e8{lim}_{s\\to 0}(4{s}^{7}+13),\\,{lim}_{s\\to 0}2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061s,\\,{lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{{s}^{2}+13}{{e}^{s}}\u27e9\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one-by-one.\n\n- For the first component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}(4{s}^{7}+13) & =4(0)^{7}+13=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061s & =2\\operatorname{sin}\u20610 \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third component, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{s\\to 0}\\frac{{s}^{2}+13}{{e}^{s}} & =\\frac{{0}^{2}+13}{{e}^{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{1} \\\\  & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{s\\to 0}f(s)=\u27e813,0,13\u27e9.$",
